  "id": "COMPOUND:31601 - PROTEIN:4970",
  "verbalization": "Arundinol B appears to exert its biological effects through a multi-step pathway that ultimately targets CCRF-HSB-2. The evidence suggests that Arundinol B directly interacts with SNU-387, which in turn is a target of Gypenoside Xlvi and Thelephantin K. These compounds are implicated in the regulation of CCRF-HSB-2, indicating a potential role in modulating cellular processes through these intermediaries. The integration of multiple pathways highlights the complexity of the interaction network, where Arundinol B may influence CCRF-HSB-2 via the activation of downstream targets that are involved in cellular signaling or metabolic pathways. The consistent presence of CCRF-HSB-2 as a target across different pathways underscores the significance of this cell line in the context of the observed effects, suggesting a possible role in drug response or therapeutic outcome.",
